      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly, I can help with that. Here's a step-by-step guide for implementing hardware security keys like Yubikeys:\n\n1. **Planning:**\n   - Assess office-wide that hardware security keys are needed.\n   - Define a rollout schedule that minimizes disruption.\n\n2. **Procurement:**\n   - Purchase a sufficient quantity of compatible Yubikeys for all employees.\n   - Order backup keys for heightened security.\n\n3. **Deployment:**\n   - Train an IT team to install and set up Yubikeys on each company's computer.\n   - Place Yubikeys in either a USB port or, for added security, unlock a secure physical box.\n\n4. **Installation and Configuration:**\n   - Ensure the necessary software or drivers accompany the Yubikeys if applicable (typically this is minimal or non-existent as Yubikeys are intended to function with built-in hardware support).\n   - Follow the on-screen instructions upon plugging in a Yubikey to enable firmware updates if needed.\n\n5. **Onboarding:**\n   - Create a standardized onboarding process, helping each employee connect their Yubikey and complete their initial setup.\n   - Reinforce a change because Yubikeys, unlike SMS-based MFA, require",
